{"id":"assistant-86c2d6f2-e951-5577-8d79-0d4c52be4606","sessionId":"b695143c-e919-c81d-c8b9-aabc565ab1dd","turnId":"turn-e7203e1e4dd9260dfbf87099ba2fa785","inputEntryId":"user-turn-e7203e1e4dd9260dfbf87099ba2fa785-1","createdAt":1794274138664,"updatedAt":1794274138664,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Cause**: The `similarity()` function in `src/app.py` returns a Python `float` via `round()`. DynamoDB rejects float types. The first publish works because the table is empty (no similarity scores computed). The second publish fails because there's now existing data, similarity scores are computed as floats, and `put_item()` rejects them.\n\n**Fix**:\n1. Added `from decimal import Decimal` to `src/app.py`\n2. Changed `similarity()` to return `Decimal(str(round(...)))` instead of a float\n3. Added `test_publish_with_existing_story` to `tests/test_publish.py` that seeds the table with one record before publishing a second story\n\nThe colleague's note applied completely: same error, same root cause, same fix pattern, and same test strategy. All details are in `ANSWER.md`."}],"source":"harness","userDisplayContent":null,"outcome":{"type":"committed"}}
